<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">repair</ansi>

A stone golem does not mend on its own: rest, camp and the trickle between
fights do nothing for it (<ansi fg="command">help stone-golem</ansi>). It is repaired with stone mortar.

  <ansi fg="command">company repair</ansi>            who needs repair, and how much mortar is in reach
  <ansi fg="command">company repair [golem]</ansi>    pack mortar into the golem until it is whole

Each mortar restores half the golem's maximum health. Mortar is taken from
the company's cargo (your own pack too, when the company keeps no shared
cargo), then from each companion's pack, and one is spent at a time until the
golem is whole or the mortar runs out. Only what is needed is used.

  - The golem must be alive and with you. A fallen golem needs a
    resurrection (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>).
  - You cannot repair in a fight or a battle (<ansi fg="command">help battle-summary</ansi>).
  - Repair takes no game time. Healing spells also heal a golem.
  - Mortar is sold at the Dunmar market for a few gold. Only the living
    mend by <ansi fg="command">heal</ansi> and rest: a hound is not repaired (<ansi fg="command">help heal</ansi>).
